.TH NA_HAMLIB_BRIDGE 1 "2026-08-30" "naudio" "naudio manual"
.SH NAME
na_hamlib_bridge \- bridge a Hamlib rig_stream audio stream onto the naudio wire
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B na_hamlib_bridge
.RB [ \-m
.IR model ]
.RB [ \-r
.IR host:port ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR naudio_port ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR channels ]
.RB [ \-R
.IR lan | wan | ft8 ]
.RB [ \-S
.IR stream_mode ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.RB [ \-x ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B na_hamlib_bridge
re-originates a Hamlib
.BR rig_stream_ *
audio stream onto naudio's FEC-native wire, so rig audio survives a lossy
LAN/WAN hop.
It runs at the radio site, upstream of that hop: Hamlib talks to the rig
(directly, or via
.BR rigctld (1)
over netrigctl), and the bridge serves the rig's RX audio as a naudio
stream while feeding client TX audio back to the rig.
.PP
The streaming subsystem it is built on is Hamlib PR #2116 (Hamlib 5.0+),
which no released Hamlib ships yet \(em the bridge must be linked against a
streaming-capable libhamlib, and as of this writing no real radio backend
implements
.IR stream_caps ,
so real-rig behaviour is unverified.
The Dummy backend (model 1) exercises the full path hardware-free.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " model"
Hamlib model number (default 1 = DUMMY, hardware-free; 2 = NETRIGCTL).
.TP
.BI \-r " host:port"
netrigctl target for model 2, e.g. localhost:5555.
.TP
.BI \-S " stream_mode"
backend stream_mode configuration.
The Dummy backend accepts
.IR tone ,
.IR silence ,
.IR loopback ,
.IR counter ;
.I loopback
feeds TX back out of RX \(em a hardware-free TX round trip.
.TP
.BI \-p " naudio_port"
port the bridge's naudio server listens on (default 4533).
.TP
.BI \-c " channels"
1 or 2 (default 1).
Stereo over netrigctl needs a libhamlib at or after Hamlib commit
961093f2 on
.B this
side; the bridge prints the applicable advice when it detects RX gaps.
.TP
.BI \-R " lan\fR|\fPwan\fR|\fPft8"
naudio reliability profile (default wan, with FEC).
.TP
.B \-k
key the rig's PTT around client TX bursts.
.TP
.B \-x
disable the TX (operator-to-rig) direction; RX only.
.TP
.B \-h
print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
clean run.
.TP
.B 1
startup or streaming failure.
.TP
.B 2
usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Hardware-free end to end, serving a test tone from the Dummy rig:
.PP
.nf
.RS
na_hamlib_bridge \-m 1 \-S tone
.RE
.fi
.PP
Bridge a remote rigctld, RX only, FT8-tuned reliability:
.PP
.nf
.RS
na_hamlib_bridge \-m 2 \-r radio\-host:5555 \-x \-R ft8
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR na_audio_daemon (1),
.BR na_wav_tap (1),
.BR rigctld (1)
.PP
Building the streaming libhamlib this tool needs, and why a skipped build
looks like a broken flag:
.I docs/hamlib\-streaming\-bridge.md
in the naudio source tree
(https://github.com/KJ5HST\-LABS/naudio).
